Step 2: We can set up a system of equations:
Step 3: \begin{align*}
Step 4: 4p + 3c &= 224 \\
Step 5: 2p + 5c &= 154
Step 6: \end{align*}
Step 7: We can multiply the second equation by 2 to eliminate $p$:
Step 8: \begin{align*}
Step 9: 4p + 10c &= 308 \\
Step 10: 4p + 3c &= 224
Step 11: \end{align*}
Step 12: Subtracting the second equation from the first, we get $7c = 84$, so $c = \boxed{12}$.
Final answer: 12

